// PengyOS Desktop - the right-click "Upscale" actions in COSMIC Files.
//
// Installed by the realesrgan-ncnn-vulkan recipe to
//   /usr/share/cosmic/com.system76.CosmicFiles/v1/context_actions
// which is cosmic-config's system default for that key: libcosmic reads
// ~/.config/cosmic/com.system76.CosmicFiles/v1/context_actions first and only
// falls back to this file (Config::get -> get_local, then get_system_default),
// so every user gets the actions with nothing written in their home, and a
// user who defines their own actions replaces this list wholesale.
//
// cosmic-files has had user-defined context actions since epoch 1.0.10
// (src/context_action.rs: name, confirm, selection, steps). The pinned
// Desktop set (epoch 1.9) has the file, so this works with no patch.
//
// selection: Files = the entry shows when the selection contains no folder.
// There is no MIME filter in cosmic-files, so the entry is offered on a .txt
// as well; pengyos-upscale refuses formats the engine cannot decode (exit 2)
// and says so in a notification, which is the guard.
//
// steps lines are parsed like a .desktop Exec and run with no shell: absolute
// paths only, no ~, no $HOME, no globs, no pipes. %F hands the whole selection
// to one invocation (%f would start one process per file). The action shows no
// output window, so the wrapper reports through notify-send.
[
    (
        name: "Upscale 2×",
        confirm: false,
        selection: Files,
        steps: ["/usr/bin/pengyos-upscale -s 2 %F"],
    ),
    (
        name: "Upscale 4×",
        confirm: false,
        selection: Files,
        steps: ["/usr/bin/pengyos-upscale -s 4 %F"],
    ),
]
